sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: The square on the second bimedial straight line applied to a rational straight line produces as breadth the third binomial.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be a second bimedial straight line divided into its medials at {C}, so that {AC} is the greater segment, let {DE} be any rational straight line, and to {DE} let there be applied the parallelogram {DF} equal to the square on {AB} and producing {DG} as its breadth.

I say that {DG} is a third binomial straight line.

Make the same construction as shown before.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="210" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.62 diagram" src="propX60.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure (X.60's): the second bimedial AB divided at C, the
    // rational DE, the rectangle DF (EDGF) applied to DE with breadth DG,
    // and inside it DH (EDKH) equal to the square on AC, KL (HKML) equal to
    // the square on CB, MG bisected at N and the parallel NO. "Make the same
    // construction as shown before" is one slide that rebuilds it.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: a solid twin DE (initiallyHidden) so the
    // rational line stands when set out, before DF is applied; transparent
    // targets AC, CB, DG, DM, MG, ML, DK, KM, MN (;0;0;0); faceless twins
    // DFh, DHh, KLh, DLh (E,D,M,L) and MFh (L,M,G,F), since the random-faced
    // rectangles would be raised over the figure when lit (#140), reached
    // through the aliases DF, DH, KL, DL, MF. No angle is called right.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, D, E (line sliders)
    // and the offscreen frees. C arrives with "divided into its medials at
    // C", D and E with "let DE be any rational straight line", so all three
    // are deferred. G, F, K, H, M, L, N, O are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","AB"];
    var MEDS  = GIVEN.concat(["C","AC","CB"]);
    var RAT   = MEDS.concat(["D","E","DE"]);
    var APP   = RAT.concat(["G","F","EDGF","DFh","DG"]);
    var ALL   = APP.concat(["K","H","EDKH","M","L","HKML","N","O","NO",
                            "DHh","KLh","DLh","MFh","DM","MG","ML","DK","KM","MN"]);
