            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,170,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,120,0",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "D;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,0,40",
            "E;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,0,130",
            "G';point;parallelogram;D,A0,A3;0;0",
            "G;point;proportion;D,E,A,B,A,B,D,G'",
            "F;point;parallelogram;E,D,G",
            "EDGF;polygon;quadrilateral;E,D,G,F;0;0;black;random",
            "K;point;proportion;D,E,A,C,A,C,D,G'",
            "EDKH;polygon;parallelogram;E,D,K;0;0;black;random",
            "H;point;vertex;EDKH,4",
            "M;point;proportion;D,E,B,C,B,C,K,G'",
            "HKML;polygon;parallelogram;H,K,M;0;0;black;random",
            "L;point;vertex;HKML,4",
            "N;point;midpoint;M,G",
            "O;point;parallelogram;E,D,N",
            "NO;line;connect;N,O",
            // Slide-only twins and highlight targets.
            "DE;line;connect;D,E",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C;0;0;0",
            "CB;line;connect;C,B;0;0;0",
            "DG;line;connect;D,G;0;0;0",
            "DM;line;connect;D,M;0;0;0",
            "MG;line;connect;M,G;0;0;0",
            "ML;line;connect;M,L;0;0;0",
            "DK;line;connect;D,K;0;0;0",
            "KM;line;connect;K,M;0;0;0",
            "MN;line;connect;M,N;0;0;0",
            "DFh;polygon;quadrilateral;E,D,G,F;0;0;0;0",
            "DHh;polygon;quadrilateral;E,D,K,H;0;0;0;0",
            "KLh;polygon;quadrilateral;H,K,M,L;0;0;0;0",
            "DLh;polygon;quadrilateral;E,D,M,L;0;0;0;0",
            "MFh;polygon;quadrilateral;L,M,G,F;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["DE"],
        deferDraggables: ["C","D","E"],
        aliases: { "DF": "DFh", "DH": "DHh", "KL": "KLh", "DL": "DLh",
                   "MF": "MFh", "MD": "DM" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“The square on the second bimedial straight line applied to a rational straight line",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","DE","DFh"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.62" }] },
            { text: "produces as breadth the third binomial.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DG"] },
            { text: "Let {AB} be a second bimedial straight line",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "divided into its medials at {C}, so that {AC} is the greater segment,",
              visible: MEDS,
              highlighted: ["C","AC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "C", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "let {DE} be any rational straight line,",
              visible: RAT,
              highlighted: ["DE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "D",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "DE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "and to {DE} let there be applied the parallelogram {DF} equal to the square on {AB}",
              visible: APP,
              highlighted: ["DE","AB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "EDGF", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and producing {DG} as its breadth.",
              visible: APP,
              highlighted: ["DG"] },
            { text: "I say that {DG} is a third binomial straight line.",
              visible: APP,
              highlighted: ["DG"] },
            { text: "Make the same construction as shown before.",
              visible: ALL,
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "K",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "EDKH", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "M",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "HKML", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "N",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "NO",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Then, since {AB} is a second bimedial divided at {C},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","C"] },
            { text: "therefore {AC} and {CB} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only and containing a medial rectangle,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB a second bimedial", ref: "X.38" }] },
            { text: "so that the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.15" }, { ref: "X.23.Cor" }] },
            { text: "And it equals {DL}, therefore {DL} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DLh"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {DE},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DLh","DE"] },
            { text: "therefore {MD} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {DE}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DM","DE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DM rational, incommensurable with DE", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason, {MG} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {ML}, that is, with {DE},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MFh","MG","ML","DE"] },
            { text: "therefore each of the straight lines {DM} and {MG} is rational and incommensurable in length with {DE}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DM","MG","DE"] },
            { text: "Since {AC} is incommensurable in length with {CB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "and {AC} is to {CB} as the square on {AC} is to the rectangle {AC} by {CB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {AC} is also incommensurable with the rectangle {AC} by {CB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "square incommensurable with rectangle", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "Hence the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.12" }, { ref: "X.13" }] },
            { text: "that is, {DL} is incommensurable with {MF}, so that {DM} is also incommensurable with {MG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DLh","MFh","DM","MG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DL : MF = DM : MG", ref: "VI.1" },
                               { claim: "DM, MG incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "And they are rational, therefore {DG} is binomial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DM","MG","DG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DG binomial", ref: "X.36" }] },
            { text: "It is to be proved that it is a third binomial straight line.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DG"] },
            { text: "In manner similar to the foregoing we may conclude that {DM} is greater than {MG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DM","MG"] },
            { text: "and that {DK} is commensurable with {KM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DK","KM"] },
            { text: "And the rectangle {DK} by {KM} equals the square on {MN},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DK","KM","MN"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {DM} is greater than the square on {MG}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DM","MG"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line commensurable with {DM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DM"] },
            { text: "And neither of the straight lines {DM} nor {MG} is commensurable in length with {DE}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DM","MG","DE"] },
            { text: "Therefore {DG} is a third binomial straight line.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "third binomial", ref: "X.Def.II.3" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, the square on the second bimedial straight line applied to a rational straight line",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","DE","DFh"] },
            { text: "produces as breadth the third binomial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DG"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.62") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "VI.1":       "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "X.11":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.12":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX12/",
        "X.13":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX13/",
        "X.15":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX15/",
        "X.22":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX22/",
        "X.23.Cor":   "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX23/#cor",
        "X.36":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX36/",
        "X.38":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX38/",
        "X.Def.II.3": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.II.3/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Then, since {AB} is a second bimedial divided at {C}, therefore {AC} and {CB} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only and containing a medial rectangle, so that the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is also medial. [!just X.38; X.15; X.23.Cor]

And it equals {DL}, therefore {DL} is also medial. And it is applied to the rational straight line {DE}, therefore {MD} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {DE}. [!just X.22]

For the same reason, {MG} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {ML}, that is, with {DE}, therefore each of the straight lines {DM} and {MG} is rational and incommensurable in length with {DE}.

Since {AC} is incommensurable in length with {CB}, and {AC} is to {CB} as the square on {AC} is to the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, therefore the square on {AC} is also incommensurable with the rectangle {AC} by {CB}. [!just X.11]

Hence the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, that is, {DL} is incommensurable with {MF}, so that {DM} is also incommensurable with {MG}. [!just X.12, X.13; VI.1, X.11]

And they are rational, therefore {DG} is binomial. [!just X.36]

It is to be proved that it is a third binomial straight line.

In manner similar to the foregoing we may conclude that {DM} is greater than {MG}, and that {DK} is commensurable with {KM}.

And the rectangle {DK} by {KM} equals the square on {MN}, therefore the square on {DM} is greater than the square on {MG} by the square on a straight line commensurable with {DM}. And neither of the straight lines {DM} nor {MG} is commensurable in length with {DE}.

Therefore {DG} is a third binomial straight line. [!just X.Def.II.3]

Therefore, *the square on the second bimedial straight line applied to a rational straight line produces as breadth the third binomial.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
